WEBVTT

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:11.640
Enemy units approaching from Point 211!

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.170
Follow me in T-Formation!

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.970
What are you doing?!

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:18.340
How many defeats until you're happy?!
That's your 10th one now!

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.010
And you call yourselves Reasoners?!

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:24.310
But it ain't gonna be that easy
to master fighting other Strains!

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:26.620
Excuses are worthless in real combat!

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.720
You need to cope with everything better!

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.420
If you can't do that,
get out of your Strains!

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:34.180
That is all for today! Dismissed!

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.030
Cope with everything, huh...

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.500
It's like, "Why don't you
show us how it's done, then?!"

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.630
Right, Carris?

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:47.070
Well, it is true that our normal
methods don't have any effect on it.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:50.310
Aside from the Queen,
she was the only other person

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.080
who was on even terms with
that Strain the other day...

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:57.980
But no matter how mobile her unit is,
if she ignores formation...

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:01.450
We need a new formation
for use against Strains.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.320
Eh?!

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:06.790
We're the only Reasoners
who survived that last battle.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.190
As such, the most skilled should
take the center of the formation.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.560
That is the only way
to protect our friends' lives.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:17.000
So there you have it!
Understand, Gutsy Girl?!

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:22.340
Hey! Do you hear me?! At least respond!

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.670
Alright, you! Listen here-

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.670
Good work again today, Emily.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:37.520
Endless Love and Hate

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.570
Three minutes until completion
of Deceleration Sequence #4.

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.010
Engines green. All ships normal.

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.750
No enemies detected within sensor range.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:59.750
We can only hope we've
escaped the enemy now...

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:03.020
That is all we can have faith in for now.

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:07.520
Until we reach the Gall
Space Supply Depot, at least.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.830
What have we learned about
Sara Cruz since then?

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.260
An investigation is still ongoing,

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:17.000
but there are no signs of her personal
data having been tampered with.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.840
At the very least, she is
a simple, ordinary cadet

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.840
according to this ship's records.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.440
However, because she has
done the unordinary,

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.210
it would be wise to suspect
that information.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:32.080
There's her, and then there's
that inexplicable Deague attack...

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:35.220
What exactly has this
exercise voyage turned into?

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:40.550
One minute until deceleration
sequence completion.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.160
You have such beautiful skin!

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:56.940
But I'm not lacking in
the skin department, myself!

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.510
I'm so smooth!

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:02.440
Here, you can feel, too!

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.000
Sara-san?

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:07.940
Huh?

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:15.260
Oh, that's no good!

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:19.630
You shouldn't eat the C Lunch!
I fully recommend the B Lunch!

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:24.130
Forget that! The A Lunch is where it's at!

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.330
Meat! Gotta have meat!

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.710
No, no! Girls need to eat B Lunches!

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:35.940
They're low on calories and fat,
so they're perfect for dieting!

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.350
Get real! You can't fight
on an empty stomach!

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:43.690
Whatever, Martha. All you care
about is growing muscle.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:47.220
You got too little muscle,
Ermy! Eat meat! Meat!

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.590
--Wanna split some of mine?
--No thanks!

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:52.590
--Don't be like that!
--I'm done now.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.830
You're done eating already?

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:57.930
I'll take it, then!
You should have some too, Ermy!

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:01.530
Are you trying to turn me into a pig?!
But I will take her dessert!

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:04.370
Whoops.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.900
Sorry, Sara. Are you alright?

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:14.410
S-say. If there's anything bothering you,
you can talk to me about it.

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:19.190
Why?

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:22.160
Why does everyone come up to me?

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.890
What do you mean, why? Isn't it obvious?

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:28.560
Because you're a fellow member
of the Spatial Armor Division!

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.840
Whew...

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:36.970
You sure got a formidable
one this time around!

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:39.200
Don't be stupid. It's not like that.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:48.170
Hey! Gutsy Girl!

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:55.380
Alone as always? You're a hardcore
pain in the butt, you know that?

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:07.600
You can think whatever you like.
But I'll tell you this.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:11.470
We're friends, whose lives
are in each other's hands.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.980
20 more kilometers! Come on!

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:22.970
Eh?!

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:31.220
Friends...

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:36.760
You seem to be getting
along well with them.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:53.520
You're late, Cadet Sara Cruz!

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:55.380
Start-up tests will begin immediately!

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:56.580
Get ready!

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.550
Hey! Hey, you!

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:09.230
What, is she getting hard
of hearing or something?!

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:13.400
It's less like a hearing problem
and more like you're being ignored!

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.060
Shut up, Carmichael!

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:18.300
I'm home, Emily.

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:28.940
There, you're all pretty again.

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:34.750
You're the only friend I need...

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:39.900
I don't know why...

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:47.070
But whenever I'm with you, I feel
like I can be Sara Werec again...

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:53.440
But when I'm with everyone else,
I'm Sara Cruz... not my real self.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:58.780
I'm not fit to be their
friend as I am now...

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:17.870
What're you doing?!

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:20.670
This is precious treasure!
Handle it carefully!

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:22.330
Yeah, yeah!

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:28.240
What's this?

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:31.150
Scrap metal from the battle the other day.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.350
No! It's a mountain of treasure!

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:36.850
I'm going to recycle this
to create a new Strain!

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:39.550
As a true genius, that is my duty!

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.470
We still can't send the Strain out?!

00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:30.970
Unfortunately not.

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:34.440
Our pursuit of our target
remains unchanged,

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:39.820
but filtering the Mercurion with
our equipment will take some time.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:44.090
The current progress
of operations is at 48%.

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:47.090
Our opinion of efficient use of Mercurion

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:50.060
differs from that of the Union's, you see.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:54.150
Enough excuses!
Finish the work given to you quickly!

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:58.170
What is it?! Go already!

00:09:58.170 --> 00:09:59.860
Understood.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:10.010
So they're making a detour here to lose us?

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:14.180
All that will do is buy
them a little time...

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:17.520
But we certainly lucked out here.

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:20.920
Plus we'll be able to send
the Strain out again soon.

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:24.410
Once it's ready...
This time for sure, okay?

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:29.360
Please, Ralph... For the two of us...

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:52.350
There's nothing out of the ordinary
with any of her medical data.

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:54.760
It's all within normal parameters.

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:58.330
But why is she the only one
we're checking this closely?

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:01.400
Never mind the details.
Just do your checks.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:02.730
Yes, sir...

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:08.230
I guess the serious checks will
have to wait until we reach Gall...

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.740
I'm finding it hard to believe
this girl is a secret weapon...

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:16.980
Eh?! What do you mean
by "secret weapon"?!

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:21.180
Just shut up and do your work!
Don't make me flunk you!

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:32.390
E-mail? From who?

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:40.700
So Chie-chan from the Comms
Division just wouldn't let me!

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:44.040
Man, talk about annoying!

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:46.810
Seriously, what're you talking about?

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.330
You know what I mean!

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:54.020
Oh, Sara! Uhh, Lottie just contacted us.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:57.950
She wants us to gather
in the simulation room...

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.020
I think she hates you...

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:05.650
Don't be stupid! It'd make
sense in your case, though!

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:20.440
You're too slow!

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:23.580
Given that I called you here,
you should come faster!

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:26.150
--Whoa! Scary!
--Quit screwing around!

00:12:26.150 --> 00:12:29.520
So, what's the deal?
Why'd you suddenly call us here?

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:34.080
Yes. I've been thinking things
over since the last simulation...

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:39.190
This is our current formation, right?

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:42.900
Yes. This is with me in the top spot.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:46.600
But we can't beat Ralph Werec
and his Strain this way.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:50.670
That's why we're going to defeat
him with the following formation.

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:54.880
We'll move Sara Cruz, our rearguard,
to the top alongside me.

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:59.410
With her unit's mobility, this should
increase our offense by a lot!

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:02.220
--Sara...
--...and Lottie?

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:04.950
A Two-Top, huh...

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:10.360
Not Sara and me! Me and Sara!
Don't mix up the order!

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:13.460
But are you really sure
we should use a Two-Top?

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:16.900
I've already received approval
from Instructor Dufarge.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:21.040
Simulation data suited to this
formation is already being made.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:22.770
Do you have a problem with that?

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:23.740
N-no...

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:26.780
That's not what she means!
Are you sure about using her?!

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:29.780
To be honest, won't she have
more of a problem with teamwork

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.780
than skill and all that?

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:34.720
Yeah, she might...

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:39.150
She's not as good as me, but she's
the next best Reasoner we have.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:42.490
So I have faith in her. Plus...

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:49.060
...she somehow has the same smell as me...

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:51.070
Smells, again?

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:53.840
What're you talking about?

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:57.910
I guess it's only natural for
the Queen to talk like that. Right?

00:13:57.910 --> 00:13:59.410
I guess.

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:01.640
Speaking of which, where is Gutsy Girl?

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:03.980
Eh? Oh, she isn't here...

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.380
--Come to think of it...
--Yeah.

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:14.160
Now commencing Deceleration Sequence #6.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:18.650
I repeat, now commencing
Deceleration Sequence #6.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:47.220
You got real guts. You actually came.

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:51.890
Where's Isabella? She called me here...

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:59.400
Sorry. Isabella isn't here.

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:01.670
Isn't here?

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:04.870
She died. In that battle the other day.

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:19.420
If you had gone out in
a Strain at the start...

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:22.980
...Isabella...
Isabella wouldn't have died!

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:26.390
Say something!

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:30.530
So you're a Reasoner, huh?!
You had me completely fooled!

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:34.770
Must've felt pretty good, huh?

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:38.400
Secretly looking down
on us this whole time!

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:40.340
Get out of here!

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:43.830
--I thought you were cute, too!
--Quit acting all cocky!

00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:46.510
Get away from me!

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:59.420
Well? Now do you somewhat
understand how we feel?

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:06.660
Say something, dammit!

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:25.850
W-what's with that look?!

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:29.660
It's all your fault this happened!

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:33.090
It's... it's all your fault everyone died!

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:47.280
Why?! Why are you alive?!

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:49.980
Why did Isabella die while you...

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:53.610
While you... While you get to live?!

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.770
Quit sitting there and say something!

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.530
Talk, dammit!

00:17:14.770 --> 00:17:18.100
Satisfied now?

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:22.940
F-fuck you...

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:32.350
--C'mon, that's enough, Mariette!
--This is bad!

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:34.220
C'mon, Mariette!

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:43.220
You little...

00:17:56.810 --> 00:17:59.510
I see. So this is what's up.

00:18:00.520 --> 00:18:03.020
--T-the Spatial...
--...Armor Division...

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:07.690
See, just like I told ya! These kinds
always gather in the same place!

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:11.730
Just between you and me, I've never
seen anything like this before.

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:14.720
You can take me on, if you'd like.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.600
I take it you're done now?!

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.870
Messing with her basically means

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:30.870
you're picking a fight with all
of the Spatial Armor Division!

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:35.080
If that's what you want,
we'll take you on anytime!

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:37.750
N-no, that's not what we-

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.410
W-we're sorry!

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:54.000
I-it's her! She's the one who-
It's her fault!

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:55.900
It's because of her that Isabella-

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:59.100
You're not the only one
who lost friends in battle!

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:16.720
Why?

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:21.460
Why did you help me?

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:24.600
Why? Isn't it obvious?

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:28.840
If you got hurt, there'd be a hole
in the new formation I thought up.

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:30.390
That's all.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:34.410
Or is that not good enough, Sara?

00:19:36.510 --> 00:19:38.500
So there you have it.

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:51.530
Huh?

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:54.530
Oh, no... It's over?

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:55.560
Is it?

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:56.960
Geez, you're late!

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.730
Oh, Lavinia...

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:06.900
Whoa!

00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:12.010
Honestly... What a gutsy girl...

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:33.840
She suggests holding a welcome party.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:37.040
Emily. What should I do?

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:41.310
On the next Soukou no Strain:
Back Turned to Peace

00:20:41.310 --> 00:20:43.610
This is where I return to.
